<title>USA: St Joseph hogs off $0.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs off $0.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Wednesday, barrows and gilts were $0.50 lower. Top $52.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Very few hogs moving, only 94,000 Interior Iowa Wednesday, but dressed pork trade sharply lower. Lent season and Holiday Monday.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs    51.50-52.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs    50.00-51.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady. Top $43.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-450 lbs    43.00</p>
<p>    Boars:	 300-700 lbs    39.50</p>
<p>		     200-300 lbs    40.00</p>
</text>
